==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{af|en|Jacobi|-an}}, after {{w|Carl Gustav Jacob Jacobi}}, a German mathematician of the 19th century.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|yä-kō'-bi-un}}, {{IPA|en|/jɑːˈkəʊ.bi.ən/}}
* {{IPA|en|/d͡ʒəˈkoʊ.bi.ən/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-Jacobian.wav|a=US}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{non-gloss|Used to specify certain [[mathematical]] [[object]]s named in honour of [[w:Carl Gustav Jacob Jacobi|C.&nbsp;G.&nbsp;J. Jacobi]].}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''Jacobian''' matrix has partial derivatives as its entries.}}

